    "careersEN": "Banks (e.g., Deutsche Bank, headquartered in Frankfurt) and the Big Four audit firms (Deloitte, PwC, EY, KPMG) are typical employers. Finance and consulting are among the higher-paying paths for business graduates; in general, According to German salary surveys (e.g., StepStone), business-graduate starting salaries are roughly 38,000-40,000 EUR gross/year on average, varying by industry and region",
